      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Does every database failure produce a log with the detail? (A36, done)\nThe scenario: the backend tries to insert a duplicate order and PostgreSQL refuses it (SQLSTATE `23505`, unique key violation). The database **span** keeps `exception.type` and `db.response.status_code = 23505`; the **message** and the **stack** go to **one** error log with the same `trace_id`/`span_id` — also when the trace is not sampled (then the log's trace link opens an empty trace: filter the logs by `db_system_name` / `error_type` instead). Proof: the number of failures must equal the number of logs.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "datasource",
        "uid": "-- Mixed --"
      },
      "description": "Database error logs ÷ database spans with an error. **Target: 100%.** Use a range without pod restarts (the counter resets and the number exceeds 100%).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "noValue": "no failures in range",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red"
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.9
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.98
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "value",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "exemplar": false,
          "expr": "sum(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=~\"demo-(${lang:pipe})-(api|backend|worker)\", service_name=~\"${service:pipe}\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_CLIENT\", db_system_name=\"postgresql\", status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"} - traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=~\"demo-(${lang:pipe})-(api|backend|worker)\", service_name=~\"${service:pipe}\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_CLIENT\", db_system_name=\"postgresql\", status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"} offset $__range)",
          "hide": true,
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "spans"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\"demo-(${lang:pipe})-(api|backend|worker)\", service_name=~\"${service:pipe}\"} | severity_number >= 17 | exception_type != \"\" | (db_system_name != \"\" or scope_name = \"StaffOps.OtelHelper.Database\") [$__range]))",
          "hide": true,
          "legendFormat": "",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "refId": "records"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "expression": "$records / $spans",
          "refId": "Coverage",
          "type": "math"
        }
